;;|| NEXT >
;;
;;NOT A TEST — a recorded requirement, so the next attempt does not repeat this one.
;;
;;SCORE's UEV_LpStakeScoreContext is UNREACHABLE from this tester and the reason is a missing
;;FIXTURE, not a missing technique. Its let resolves the LP token to a native LP dptf, that to a
;;swpair, and that to its token list -- all hard reads -- before any enforce runs. Pairing an
;;existing class-1 score with an LP id (the selection trick that worked for the stake-context
;;matrix in AQP-G2) therefore cannot work here: there is no LP id to pair with.
;;
;;Measured 2026-09-10 rather than assumed: binding (ref-SWP::UR_TokenLP "W|DLK-...|OURO-...|DWK-...")
;;under a `try` returned the sentinel, and the call then died on
;;    No value found in table ouronet-ns.SWP_SWP|LP for key: MISSING
;;The weighted pool that [6.4]_AQP-TRIPLET-DIAG uses is created by suites this tester does not
;;load ([6.2]_AQP stops at [6.2.16]); AQP-FULL loads them.
;;
;;To pin it, a fixture must first issue an SWP pool AND an LP-denominated class-0 score, then the
;;guard is reachable by mismatching either the score class, the aqpool link, or the lp-denominator
;;against the pair's token list -- four conditions folded into one message, so one mismatch is
;;enough per assertion.

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "AQP-G7 — three Stage-2 argument-domain guards, including one string prefix that gates a refund")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
;;==== AQP-G7 — three Stage-2 argument-domain guards, including one string prefix that gates a refund · 01 · namespace ==== 
(print "--- [AQP-G7 — three Stage-2 argument-domain guards, including one string prefix that gates a refund · 01 · namespace] ---")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [AQP-G7 · 01 · score precision, class floor, reserved-token vacate] ---")
;;All three validate arguments only -- no table, no capability. Grouped because they belong to
;;the Stage-2 modules this suite already deploys, not because they are related.
;;
;;UEV_TrueFungibleStakeNotReserved is the one worth reading twice. It is a two-character string
;;test -- does the id start with "R|" -- and it is the only thing standing between a VACATE and
;;a RESERVED token. Reserved DPTFs are the ones a pool has locked as its own backing, so
;;vacating one would refund a user with collateral that is not theirs. A guard that cheap
;;protecting something that expensive is exactly the kind that goes untested for years.
;;==== AQP-G7 — three Stage-2 argument-domain guards, including one string prefix that gates a refund · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [AQP-G7 — three Stage-2 argument-domain guards, including one string prefix that gates a refund · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (ref-DPDC-N:module{DpdcNonceV2} DPDC-N)
        (ref-VCT:module{AcquisitionVacateV1} AQP-VCT)
    )
    (map print
        [
            ;;--- score precision: 24 decimals is the limit, so the boundary is 24 vs 25
            (expect "<<AQP-G7>> a score using exactly 24 decimals is accepted"
                true (ref-DPDC-N::UEV_Score 0.000000000000000000000001))
            (expect-failure "<<AQP-G7>> ...and a 25th decimal is refused"
                "can have up to 24 decimals precision"
                (ref-DPDC-N::UEV_Score 0.0000000000000000000000001))
            ;;--- the class floor. Zero is the value a caller gets from an uninitialised integer,
            ;;which is why the guard is (> nosc 0) and not (>= nosc 0).
            (expect-failure "<<AQP-G7>> a zero nonce-or-set-class is refused"
                "Operation requires greater than zero <nonce-or-set-class>"
                (ref-DPDC-N::UEV_NonceDataUpdater "X" false "Y" 0 false false))
            (expect-failure "<<AQP-G7>> ...and so is a negative one"
                "Operation requires greater than zero <nonce-or-set-class>"
                (ref-DPDC-N::UEV_NonceDataUpdater "X" false "Y" -1 false false))
            ;;--- reserved-token vacate. Both sides, because the guard is a PREFIX test and a
            ;;broken one that refused everything would look identical from the rejection alone.
            (expect "<<AQP-G7>> an ordinary DPTF may be vacated"
                true (ref-VCT::UEV_TrueFungibleStakeNotReserved "OURO-98c486052a51"))
            (expect-failure "<<AQP-G7>> ...but the RESERVED (R|) form of the same token may not"
                "Reserved DPTF (R|) cannot be vacated"
                (ref-VCT::UEV_TrueFungibleStakeNotReserved "R|OURO-98c486052a51"))
            ;;and the test really is on the PREFIX, not on the substring appearing anywhere --
            ;;an id that merely contains "R|" further along is still vacatable.
            (expect "<<AQP-G7>> the rule is a PREFIX test, not a substring search"
                true (ref-VCT::UEV_TrueFungibleStakeNotReserved "OUR|O-98c486052a51"))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
