(begin-tx "AQP-G8a — the stake-update arity family, reached with test-capability")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
;;==== AQP-G8a — the stake-update arity family, reached with test-capability · 01 · namespace ==== 
(print "--- [AQP-G8a — the stake-update arity family, reached with test-capability · 01 · namespace] ---")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [AQP-G8a · 01 · class-2 native DPOF nonces] ---")
;;FIVE near-identical defcaps -- one per asset kind -- each opening with the SAME structural
;;check: the nonce list and the amount list must be the same length and non-empty. A caller that
;;gets this wrong is about to credit a score for nonces it never staked, so the check is the
;;first line of every one of them.
;;
;;TECHNIQUE. These are defcaps, so the obvious route is the full Talos stake flow -- an account,
;;a funded pool, real custody. None of that is needed: `test-capability` acquires a capability
;;directly and runs its body, and this enforce sits ABOVE every read, so dummy ids reach it. That
;;makes five guards free that had been filed as "needs a stake fixture".
;;
;;BOUNDARY, worth writing down: `test-capability` does NOT work on an `@event` defcap. Pact tries
;;to INSTALL those and fails with "capability is not managed and cannot be installed". So the
;;three link caps in this module (CREATE-AQPOOL-LINK, REVOKE-AQPOOL-LINK, CREATE-FVT-LINK) are
;;NOT reachable this way and stay on the worklist -- verified, not assumed.
;;
;;EACH CASE GETS ITS OWN TRANSACTION: a granted capability is cached for the rest of the tx, so
;;re-acquiring the same one would return the grant without re-running the body.
;;
;;Each message is prefixed by its asset kind, so the five are individually attributable -- which
;;is the only reason testing all five is worth more than testing one.
(map print
    [
        (expect-failure "<<AQP-G8a>> UPDATE-STAKE-DPOF: one nonce against two amounts is refused"
            "DPOF stake score update: nonces and nonce-amounts must have equal positive length"
            (test-capability (AQP-SCORE.SCR|XE>UPDATE-STAKE-DPOF "a" "b" "c" "d" [1] [1.0 2.0] true)))
    ]
)
(commit-tx)

