(begin-tx "AQP-G9 — the three FVT stake-flow admission caps, driven by pool CLASS")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [AQP-G9 · 01 · stake-flow admission] ---")
;;FVT has one stake-flow cap per asset kind — true-fungible, orto-fungible, collectable — and each
;;opens with a short chain of pool checks. They are reachable here because this suite happens to
;;hold pools of DIFFERENT classes and admission states, which is exactly what the chain discriminates
;;on. Nothing new had to be built; the fixture was already the right shape:
;;
;;   TfStakePool   TF-class OK,  stake admission FALSE
;;   OfStakePool   TF-class NO,  stake admission true   (ortofungible pool)
;;   SfStakePool   TF-class NO,  stake admission true   (collectable pool)
;;
;;So the class guard is driven with an ORTO pool offered to the TF flow, and the admission guard
;;with the one pool that passes the class check but is not open for staking. Each case satisfies
;;the guards before it — a pool that failed both would only ever prove the first.
;;==== AQP-G9 — the three FVT stake-flow admission caps, driven by pool CLASS · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [AQP-G9 — the three FVT stake-flow admission caps, driven by pool CLASS · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(let*
    (
        (ref-U|DALOS:module{UtilityDalosV2} U|DALOS)
        (ref-AQP:module{AcquisitionPoolsV1} AQP-POOL)
        (tf:string (ref-U|DALOS::UDC_Makeid "TfStakePool"))
        (of:string (ref-U|DALOS::UDC_Makeid "OfStakePool"))
        (sf:string (ref-U|DALOS::UDC_Makeid "SfStakePool"))
    )
    (map print
        [
            ;;preconditions: the three pools really do differ the way the tests assume
            (expect "<<AQP-G9>> TfStakePool passes the TF class check; the other two do not"
                [true false false]
                [(ref-AQP::URC_StakeTrueFungiblePoolClassOk tf)
                 (ref-AQP::URC_StakeTrueFungiblePoolClassOk of)
                 (ref-AQP::URC_StakeTrueFungiblePoolClassOk sf)])
            (expect "<<AQP-G9>> ...and TfStakePool is NOT open for staking, which is what makes guard 2 reachable"
                false (ref-AQP::URC_PoolStakeAdmissionOk tf))
            ;;--- guard 1: an ortofungible pool offered to the TRUE-FUNGIBLE flow
            (expect-failure "<<AQP-G9>> a non-TF pool is refused by the true-fungible stake flow"
                "Invalid pool-id: TF stake requires aqp-class 0 or 1"
                (test-capability (AQP-FVT.FVT|C>TRUE-FUNGIBLE-STAKE-FLOW
                    of KST.ANHD KST.ANHD "OURO-98c486052a51" 1.0 true)))
            ;;--- guard 2: right class, but the pool is closed for staking
            (expect-failure "<<AQP-G9>> ...and a correctly-classed pool that is closed for staking is refused too"
                "Invalid pool-id: pool stake disabled or has no employed scores"
                (test-capability (AQP-FVT.FVT|C>TRUE-FUNGIBLE-STAKE-FLOW
                    tf KST.ANHD KST.ANHD "OURO-98c486052a51" 1.0 true)))
            ;;--- the nonce/amount arity guards on the other two flows. Both pools DO pass their
            ;;admission checks, so these reach the arity check rather than stopping short — which
            ;;is the only reason the assertions are attributable to arity at all.
            (expect-failure "<<AQP-G9>> orto flow: one nonce against two amounts is refused"
                "Invalid nonces / nonce-amounts: equal positive length required"
                (test-capability (AQP-FVT.FVT|C>ORTO-FUNGIBLE-STAKE-FLOW
                    of KST.ANHD KST.ANHD "MVST-98c486052a51" [1] [1.0 2.0] true)))
            (expect-failure "<<AQP-G9>> collectable flow: likewise"
                "Invalid nonces / nonce-amounts: equal positive length required"
                (test-capability (AQP-FVT.FVT|C>COLLECTABLE-STAKE-FLOW
                    sf KST.ANHD KST.ANHD "DHCD-98c486052a51" true [1] [1 2] true)))
            ;;--- and the son/class agreement: SfStakePool is an SFT pool, so offering it a
            ;;collectable flagged NON-semi-fungible is refused.
            (expect-failure "<<AQP-G9>> a collectable whose son flag disagrees with the pool class is refused"
                "Invalid pool-id: collectable son does not match pool aqp-class"
                (test-capability (AQP-FVT.FVT|C>COLLECTABLE-STAKE-FLOW
                    sf KST.ANHD KST.ANHD "DHCD-98c486052a51" false [1] [1] true)))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
;;NOT PINNED, and one MEASUREMENT CAVEAT worth stating plainly:
;;
;;  "Invalid pool-id: pool stake disabled or has no employed scores" appears at THREE sites in
;;  this module — once per flow — with identical text. Only the true-fungible one is driven above;
;;  the orto and collectable pools both pass their admission checks, which is what lets their
;;  arity guards be reached. The coverage tool disambiguates shared wording ACROSS modules, not
;;  WITHIN one, so it will credit all three from the single assertion. Two of those three credits
;;  are nominal. Driving them needs an orto/collectable pool that is closed for staking.
;;
;;  "Invalid dptf-id: leg does not match pool canonical asset" needs a pool that is BOTH TF-classed
;;  and open (stake or unstake) — TfStakePool is closed on both directions here, so guard 2
;;  answers first. One open TF pool would close it.
;;
;;  The three "Invalid FVT reward pipeline" guards need an employed score carrying an enabled FVT
;;  ScoreEntityLink and a reward DPTF — the same stake-ready pool the item above wants.
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "AQP-G10 — the leg guard, reached on a pool that is genuinely OPEN for staking")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [AQP-G10 · 01 · canonical-asset leg check] ---")
;;"Invalid dptf-id: leg does not match pool canonical asset" sits THIRD in the true-fungible flow,
;;so reaching it needs a pool that clears the class check AND the admission check. I had recorded
;;this as blocked on a fixture that would take several passes to build. It was not: [6.2.10]'s
;;ResumeVacPool is exactly that pool — fully vacated, auto-finalised, stake re-enabled — and this
;;suite already loads it. Asserted below rather than assumed, because the whole test depends on it.
;;
;;The guard is what stops a stake credited in one asset from being accounted against a pool
;;denominated in another. Its input is a REAL token (MOCKA) that simply is not this pool's asset,
;;not a ghost id — a ghost would also fail a dozen other ways and prove less.
;;==== AQP-G10 — the leg guard, reached on a pool that is genuinely OPEN for staking · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [AQP-G10 — the leg guard, reached on a pool that is genuinely OPEN for staking · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(let*
    (
        (ref-U|DALOS:module{UtilityDalosV2} U|DALOS)
        (ref-AQP:module{AcquisitionPoolsV1} AQP-POOL)
        (pool:string (ref-U|DALOS::UDC_Makeid "ResumeVacPool"))
    )
    (map print
        [
            (expect "<<AQP-G10>> ResumeVacPool clears BOTH gates that front the leg check"
                [true true]
                [(ref-AQP::URC_StakeTrueFungiblePoolClassOk pool)
                 (ref-AQP::URC_PoolStakeAdmissionOk pool)])
            (expect "<<AQP-G10>> ...and its canonical asset is OURO, not MOCKA"
                "OURO-98c486052a51" (ref-AQP::UR_AQP|PoolAssetId pool))
            (expect-failure "<<AQP-G10>> staking a real token that is NOT the pool's asset is refused"
                "Invalid dptf-id: leg does not match pool canonical asset"
                (test-capability (AQP-FVT.FVT|C>TRUE-FUNGIBLE-STAKE-FLOW
                    pool KST.ANHD KST.ANHD "MOCKA-98c486052a51" 1.0 true)))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(commit-tx)

