(begin-tx "AQP-G23b — ...and the common-denominator SHAPE guard, now reachable")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [AQP-G23b · 01 · common-denominator shape] ---")
;;With an unlinked farm in hand the immutability guard passes and the shape guard is finally the
;;one that answers. Both sides are pinned: a real native DPTF is accepted, BAR is not.
;;==== AQP-G23b — ...and the common-denominator SHAPE guard, now reachable · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [AQP-G23b — ...and the common-denominator SHAPE guard, now reachable · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(let*
    (
        (ref-U|DALOS:module{UtilityDalosV2} U|DALOS)
        (ref-RPS:module{AcquisitionRewardPerShareV1} RPS)
        (farm:string (ref-U|DALOS::UDC_Makeid "G23Farm"))
    )
    (map print
        [
            ;;preconditions: class 0 AND zero links are BOTH required for the shape guard to be the
            ;;one speaking — assert them, because if either were wrong a different guard answers.
            (expect "<<AQP-G23b>> G23Farm is a class-0 farm"
                0 (ref-RPS::UR_FVT|FvtClass farm))
            (expect "<<AQP-G23b>> ...with no linked score entities"
                0 (ref-RPS::UR_FVT|MemberLinkCount farm))
            (expect "<<AQP-G23b>> a real native DPTF is accepted as a common denominator"
                true (!= "" (format "{}"
                    [(AQP-FVT.UEV_SetCommonDenominatorContext farm "OURO-98c486052a51")])))
            (expect-failure "<<AQP-G23b>> ...and BAR is refused on shape, not on immutability"
                "common-denominator must be a full native DPTF id"
                (AQP-FVT.UEV_SetCommonDenominatorContext farm "|"))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
;;WHAT THIS FARM DOES **NOT** UNLOCK, checked rather than assumed:
;;
;;  "Non-mosaic FVT locked to score membership only" and its triplet twin need a non-mosaic FVT
;;      whose membership mode is neither BAR nor the matching kind. C_SetMosaic can clear mosaic on
;;      this farm (zero links, so it is permitted) — but there is NO setter for membership mode;
;;      it is assigned implicitly when the first entity is admitted. So clearing mosaic alone
;;      leaves mode at BAR and the guard still passes.
;;
;;  "Farm score: lp-denominator and ghost weight required" needs a score that passes the whole
;;      admission fold first: unlinked to any FVT, linked to a POOL, class-matched. Every score in
;;      this suite is already FVT-linked except Bloodshed, which has no pool link — so the fold
;;      answers before the farm rule. That one needs a freshly issued score, not a second farm.
(env-sigs [])
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
;;AQP-G24 — THE FRESH-SCORE FIXTURE.
;;
;;Several guards across FVT need a score that is ISSUED, POOL-LINKED and FVT-UNLINKED, and every
;;score in this suite is already FVT-linked. AQP-G23 showed that a second FVT alone does not cascade;
;;a second SCORE does. Two are issued here because the guards want different OWNERS:
;;
;;   G24Score  owned by EMMA  -> reaches "Score owner must match FVT owner" against an ANHD vault
;;   G25Score  owned by ANHD  -> passes the owner check and the admission fold, so the class-branch
;;                               rule ("Vault/Treasury score: swpair | and zero ghost weight") is
;;                               the guard that finally answers
;;
;;Both are class 1, matching SfStakeVault, and both are POOL-linked — which turns out to be load
;;bearing for a reason worth recording: UEV_AddScoreEntityScoreContext binds
;;    expected-swpair = (URC_ResolveScoreEntitySwpair ...)
;;in the `let` ABOVE its enforces, and that hard-reads the pool table via the score's aqpool-link.
;;So a score with NO pool link aborts in that read before ANY of the function's guards run —
;;including the very first one. The degradation recorded at TX-BOOT-G1 is not just a bad message:
;;it makes every guard in the function unreachable for an unlinked score. Linking both scores to a
;;pool is what gets past it.
;;
;;Both issues are ADDITIVE (new rows) and sit at the end of this file.

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "AQP-G24a — issue a fresh class-1 score owned by EMMA")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [AQP-G24a · 01 · issue G24Score] ---")
;;Owned by EMMA, so its owner differs from SfStakeVault's. EMMA must co-sign, because
;;score issuance enforces ownership of the owner-konto it is issued to.
(let*
    (
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
        (ref-TS02-C3:module{TalosStageTwo_ClientThreeV1} TS02-C3)
        (patron:string KST.ANHD)
        (ps:string (ref-DALOS::UR_AccountStoa patron))
        (dem:[string] (ref-DALOS::UR_DemiurgoiID))
        (sp:[decimal] (ref-DALOS::URC_SplitSTOAPrices patron 100.0))
    )
    (env-sigs
        [
            { "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }
            { "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }
            { "key": "6fa1d9c3e5078a54038159c9a6bd7182301e16d6f280615eddb18b8bd2d6c263",
              "caps":
                [
                    (coin.TRANSFER ps (ref-DALOS::UR_AccountStoa (at 1 dem)) (at 2 sp))
                    (coin.TRANSFER ps (ref-DALOS::UR_AccountStoa (at 2 dem)) (at 0 sp))
                    (coin.TRANSFER ps (ref-DALOS::UR_AccountStoa (ref-DALOS::GOV|OUROBOROS|SC_NAME)) (at 3 sp))
                    (coin.TRANSFER ps (ref-DALOS::UR_AccountStoa (ref-DALOS::GOV|DALOS|SC_NAME)) (at 1 sp))
                ]
            }
        ]
    )
    (ref-TS02-C3::AQP-SCR|C_IssueTrueFungibleScore patron KST.EMMA "G24Score" 3 1.0)
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(commit-tx)

