(begin-tx "AQP-G30 — score/pool assignment and revocation preconditions")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
;;==== AQP-G30 — score/pool assignment and revocation preconditions · 01 · namespace ==== =========
(print "--- [AQP-G30 — score/pool assignment and revocation preconditions · 01 · namespace] ---")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [AQP-G30 · 01 · UEV_AddScorePoolAndScore / UEV_RevokeScorePoolAndScore] ---")
;;P3.3. Two plain callable UEV_s, driven against the pools and the fresh G24Score this file already
;;builds.
;;
;;The add-side guard is a four-conjunct fold and the case below drives the LINK conjunct: G24Score
;;is already assigned to DrainVacPool, so offering it to a second pool is refused. That is the rule
;;that keeps a score's weight in exactly one pool — a score counted in two pools would have its
;;stake rewarded twice.
(let*
    (
        (ref-U|DALOS:module{UtilityDalosV2} U|DALOS)
        (ref-AQP:module{AcquisitionPoolsV1} AQP-POOL)
        (ref-SCR:module{AcquisitionScoresV1} AQP-SCORE)
        (drain:string (ref-U|DALOS::UDC_Makeid "DrainVacPool"))
        (tfp:string (ref-U|DALOS::UDC_Makeid "TfStakePool"))
        (linked:string (ref-U|DALOS::UDC_Makeid "G24Score"))
    )
    (map print
        [
            ;;preconditions: the score really is linked, and to the OTHER pool — which is what
            ;;makes the refusal below about the link rather than about a duplicate slot.
            (expect "<<AQP-G30>> G24Score is assigned to DrainVacPool, not to TfStakePool"
                [drain 1] [(ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreAqpoolLink linked) (ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreClass linked)])
            ;;--- revoke: slot-index -1 is what URC_ScoreSlotIndexForScore returns for a score that
            ;;    is not in the pool at all, so this is the "you asked to revoke something that was
            ;;    never there" case. It is checked FIRST, above the fold, precisely so the fold's
            ;;    reads are never run on a nonexistent pairing.
            (expect-failure "<<AQP-G30>> revoking a score that is not assigned to the pool is refused"
                "score-id is not assigned to pool"
                (ref-AQP::UEV_RevokeScorePoolAndScore drain linked -1))
            ;;--- add: an ALREADY-assigned score cannot be assigned again.
            (expect-failure "<<AQP-G30>> a score already assigned elsewhere cannot be added to another pool"
                "Invalid score-id for pool assignment"
                (ref-AQP::UEV_AddScorePoolAndScore tfp linked 1))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(commit-tx)
;;FINDING — the add-side fold's FIRST conjunct is dead. It reads
;;    (= (ref-SCR::UR_SCR|ScoreScoreId score-id) score-id)
;;which is meant to catch a score that does not exist, and the guard's own message lists
;;"missing score" first among its causes. But UR_SCR|ScoreScoreId is a HARD read of SCR|T|Score,
;;so a nonexistent id aborts with
;;    No value found in table ouronet-ns.AQP-SCORE_SCR|T|Score for key: <id>
;;before the fold is evaluated. Confirmed by probe, not assumed. The named cause can therefore
;;never produce the named message — same shape as the PYTHIA / FVT / DALOS / OUROBOROS instances
;;catalogued in memories/2026-09-11-*. Fixing it needs a NEW with-default-read existence reader
;;hoisted above the fold — AQP-SCORE has no URC_ScoreExists today (only URC_TripletExists and
;;URC_ScoreEntityModelExists), and URC_TripletExists is the precedent: its own source comment says
;;it was written as a with-default-read precisely so it could answer for a missing row, after the
;;identical defect was found and fixed in UEV_AddScoreEntityTripletContext.
;;
;;NOT PINNED — the CLASS conjunct of the same fold, and UEV_AddScorePoolAndScore's class-0
;;lp-denominator guard, both need a class mismatch to be constructible. Every pool in this suite is
;;class 1, 2, 3 or 4 and every score matches its pool's class, so no mismatched pair exists. The
;;lp-denominator rule additionally applies only when aqp-class = 0, and a class-0 pool needs a real
;;SWP **LP token** as its asset — this tester runs the ISSUANCE-ONLY Stage-1 path, which creates no
;;swap pairs at all (probed: SWP|Pairs has no row for the Stage-1 stable pool). So the fixture is
;;not "one more pool" here; it needs the full SWP path loaded first.

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "AQP-G31 — FIXED: two RPS folds that were defeated by their own later conjunct")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [AQP-G31 · 01 · fold (and) is not short-circuiting -- now hoisted] ---")
;;P3.3, pinned AS IT BEHAVES, because the written messages cannot fire.
;;
;;`fold` receives an ALREADY-BUILT list, so EVERY conjunct of (fold (and) true [...]) is evaluated
;;before `and` runs. Verified directly rather than inferred:
;;    (enforce (fold (and) true [false (enforce false "LATER-CONJUNCT-EVALUATED")]) "FOLD-MSG")
;;    => got 'LATER-CONJUNCT-EVALUATED'
;;That is normally harmless — the conjuncts are independent predicates. It is a DEFECT when a later
;;conjunct HARD-READS a table with the very value an earlier conjunct is checking for BAR.
;;
;;RPS UEV_AddRewardLinkContext (04_RPS.pact:2957) is exactly that:
;;    [(!= multiplet-family-id BAR) (URC_MultipletFamilyExists …) (UR_FVT-MF|Active …) …]
;;UR_FVT-MF|Active is a bare `read` of FVT|T|MultipletFamily, so passing BAR — the case the FIRST
;;conjunct exists to reject — aborts in that read. The caller never sees the written message.
;;UEV_QualitySplitContext (:2992) has the same shape through the link's stored family id.
;;
;;Both are pinned here on the behaviour a caller actually gets, so a fix has to update these lines
;;deliberately. The fix for both: hoist the BAR check into its own enforce above the fold, or read
;;the family through a with-default-read (the pattern UR_FVT-SEL|ScoreEntityLink already uses, whose
;;@doc says "absent rows read as disabled" — which is why its sibling conjuncts are SAFE).
;;==== AQP-G31 — FIXED: two RPS folds that were defeated by their own later conjunct · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [AQP-G31 — FIXED: two RPS folds that were defeated by their own later conjunct · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(let*
    (
        (ref-U|DALOS:module{UtilityDalosV2} U|DALOS)
        (ref-RPS:module{AcquisitionRewardPerShareV1} RPS)
        (vault:string (ref-U|DALOS::UDC_Makeid "TfStakeVault"))
        (ouro:string (ref-U|DALOS::UDC_Makeid "OURO"))
        (dlk:string (ref-U|DALOS::UDC_Makeid "DLK"))
    )
    (map print
        [
            ;;preconditions. (vault,DLK) has NO reward link, so UEV_AddRewardLinkContext gets past
            ;;its first enforce; (vault,OURO) HAS one and it is PLAIN, which is what makes the
            ;;quality-split case reach its second enforce rather than its first.
            (expect "<<AQP-G31>> (vault,DLK) has no reward link; (vault,OURO) has a PLAIN one"
                [false true "PLAIN"]
                [(ref-RPS::URC_FvtRpsGlobalRowExists vault dlk)
                 (ref-RPS::URC_FvtRpsGlobalRowExists vault ouro)
                 (ref-RPS::UR_FVT-RG|RewardKind vault ouro)])
            ;;--- FIXED 2026-09-12. Both of these used to abort on a raw table key. The cause was the
            ;;    same in each: `fold` builds its whole list BEFORE `and` runs, so a conjunct that is
            ;;    already false saves nothing, and a later element that hard-reads
            ;;    FVT|T|MultipletFamily with a BAR id killed the transaction first. The discriminating
            ;;    check is now HOISTED out of each fold into its own enforce above it.
            ;;    Both directions matter and both are driven: the hoisted check answers for the BAR /
            ;;    PLAIN input, and the fold below it still answers for everything else (AQP-G38/G39
            ;;    and GT-12 drive those).
            (expect-failure "<<AQP-G31>> a MULTIPLET_BASE link with a BAR family is named, not a table key"
                "MULTIPLET_BASE reward requires a MultipletFamily id, not BAR"
                (ref-RPS::UEV_AddRewardLinkContext vault dlk "MULTIPLET_BASE" "|"))
            (expect-failure "<<AQP-G31>> ...and a quality split on a PLAIN link is told it is not a ladder"
                "Quality split requires a MULTIPLET_BASE reward"
                (ref-RPS::UEV_QualitySplitContext vault ouro "HOMOGENEOUS" [1000 0 0] [1000 0 0] [1000 0 0]))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(commit-tx)
;;A THIRD instance of the same shape, NOT pinnable here and worse in kind: 04_RPS.pact:3876, inside
;;XE_XI_SettleScoreRps' per-plan map, guards [(!= fvt-id BAR) … (= (UR_FVT|FvtClass fvt-id) 0) …]
;;where UR_FVT|FvtClass is a bare read of FVT|T|RewardAggregate. That fold sits in an `if`, not an
;;`enforce`, so the consequence is not a mute message — a plan carrying a BAR fvt-id would abort the
;;WHOLE batch settle instead of being skipped, which is precisely what the (!= fvt-id BAR) conjunct
;;was written to prevent. Latent rather than live (the plan builder does not emit BAR today), so
;;there is no input to drive it from here; flagged by REPL/tools/_foldeager.py.

