(begin-tx "AQP-VAC-GAS -- FullVacate must stay inside one transaction")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 1000000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== AQP-VAC-GAS -- FullVacate must stay inside one transaction · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== =====
(print "--- [AQP-VAC-GAS -- FullVacate must stay inside one transaction · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(print "--- [AQP-VAC-GAS . 01 . single-tx budget] ---")
;;CC_FullVacate's @doc calls it an "AGNOSTIC single-tx full vacate". That is a COST claim, and
;;nothing was checking it. `python3 tools/_heavy.py` [scan-budget] flags it because its static tree
;;reaches TEN heavy readers -- which would be ~400,000 gas if they all ran, far over Kadena's
;;150,000 per-tx limit, and the reason the batched CCp_Batch* slices exist beside it.
;;
;;They do not all run: the function dispatches on aqp-class and one call takes ONE branch. Measured
;;here rather than argued. A table scan costs ~40,000 gas flat (pinned in modules/STAGE-Z.repl
;;STAGEZ-17), so the figure below is about one scan plus its writes -- the doc's claim is TRUE.
;;
;;This is a REGRESSION GUARD, not a discovery. The risk is a future edit adding a second asset-lane
;;scan to a branch: still correct, still passing every functional test, and silently unable to fit
;;in a transaction on mainnet. The bound is deliberately generous (100,000, two thirds of the limit)
;;so it catches a real structural change and not gas-schedule drift.
(let* ((pool:string (U|DALOS.UDC_Makeid "ResumeVacPool"))
       (g0:integer (env-gas)))
    (TS02-C3.AQP-POOL|CC_FullVacate KST.ANHD pool)
    (let ((used:integer (- (env-gas) g0)))
        (print (format "CC_FullVacate used {} gas (limit 150000, guard 100000)" [used]))
        (map print
            [
                (expect "<<AQP-VAC-GAS>> a full vacate fits in ONE transaction, as its @doc claims"
                    true (< used 100000))
                ;;and it really did the work -- otherwise a no-op would pass the budget trivially
                (expect "<<AQP-VAC-GAS>> ...and it did real work (not a no-op that passes cheaply)"
                    true (> used 1000))
            ]
        )
    )
)
(commit-tx)

