(begin-tx "AQP-G35 — the three anchor-admission guards, and a label that is an object")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
;;==== AQP-G35 — the three anchor-admission guards, and a label that is an object · 01 · namespace ==== 
(print "--- [AQP-G35 — the three anchor-admission guards, and a label that is an object · 01 · namespace] ---")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [AQP-G35 · 01 · boost-class active, 7-anchor slot, 49-anchor asset cap] ---")
;;Three unpinned guards, all of them a single field read, all of them needing state no suite reaches:
;;an INACTIVE boost class, a class with all 7 slots taken, and an asset at its 49-anchor cap. Filling
;;49 anchors through the real path would be 49 issuances; writing the counter is the same state.
;;Pattern and its boundary: 2026-09-12-state-driven-guard-coverage.md. Rolled back, with AQP-G36 as
;;the leakage check.
;;
;;ORDER MATTERS HERE and got this wrong on the first attempt: UEV_IssueAnchor checks active, then the
;;7-slot, then the 49-cap, so a leftover `anchors: 7` from the previous case SHADOWS the cap guard and
;;the assertion passes for the wrong reason. Each case therefore restores the field it changed before
;;the next one runs, and the 49-cap case is asserted through BOTH functions that carry it.
(env-module-admin AQP-ANK)
;;==== AQP-G35 — the three anchor-admission guards, and a label that is an object · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [AQP-G35 — the three anchor-admission guards, and a label that is an object · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (bc:string "TfStakeBoost-98c486052a51")
        (as:string "OURO-98c486052a51")
    )
    (map print
        [
            ;;baseline: the class is active with 1 of 7 slots used, the asset has 2 of 49 anchors.
            ;;Asserted so each refusal below is attributable to the one field that changed.
            (expect "<<AQP-G35>> baseline: class active, 1 slot used, asset at 2 anchors"
                [true 1 2]
                [(at "class-active" (AQP-ANK.UR_BC|Data bc))
                 (at "anchors" (AQP-ANK.UR_BC|Data bc))
                 (at "anchors-active" (AQP-ANK.UR_AA|Data as))])
            (expect "<<AQP-G35>> ...so both admission guards pass"
                [true true]
                [(AQP-ANK.UEV_IssueAnchor as bc) (AQP-ANK.UEV_AssetAnchorCap as)])
        ]
    )
    ;;--- guard 1: an INACTIVE boost class admits nothing
    (update AQP-ANK.ANK|T|BoostClass bc { "class-active" : false })
    (print
        (expect-failure "<<AQP-G35>> an inactive BoostClass refuses new anchors"
            "BoostClass TfStakeBoost-98c486052a51 must be active"
            (AQP-ANK.UEV_IssueAnchor as bc)))
    ;;--- guard 2: all 7 slots taken. Restore `class-active` first, or this passes on guard 1.
    (update AQP-ANK.ANK|T|BoostClass bc { "class-active" : true, "anchors" : 7 })
    (print
        (expect-failure "<<AQP-G35>> a BoostClass with all 7 slots taken refuses a new anchor"
            "BoostClass TfStakeBoost-98c486052a51 full (7 anchors)"
            (AQP-ANK.UEV_IssueAnchor as bc)))
    ;;...and 6 is still admissible, so the bound is exactly 7 and not "anchors > 1"
    (update AQP-ANK.ANK|T|BoostClass bc { "anchors" : 6 })
    (print
        (expect "<<AQP-G35>> ...while 6 of 7 is still admissible, so the bound is exactly 7"
            true (AQP-ANK.UEV_IssueAnchor as bc)))
    ;;--- guard 3: the asset-wide 49-anchor cap. `anchors` is back under the slot limit, so this is
    ;;    the only guard left that can answer.
    (update AQP-ANK.ANK|T|AssetAnchors as { "anchors-active" : 49 })
    (map print
        [
            (expect-failure "<<AQP-G35>> an asset at the 49-anchor cap refuses a new anchor"
                "Asset OURO-98c486052a51 at 49-anchor cap"
                (AQP-ANK.UEV_IssueAnchor as bc))
            ;;THE SAME MESSAGE, from a DIFFERENT function. UEV_AssetAnchorCap is the acnoi=true path
            ;;(new boost class, so there is no class row to check yet) and repeats the cap test
            ;;verbatim. Both are asserted because the wording is shared WITHIN the module: a pin on
            ;;one credits the other in `_enforce_coverage.py`, so only driving both actually tests
            ;;both. This is what that tool's "credited via text shared WITHIN one module" counts.
            (expect-failure "<<AQP-G35>> ...and the acnoi=true path repeats the cap, word for word"
                "Asset OURO-98c486052a51 at 49-anchor cap"
                (AQP-ANK.UEV_AssetAnchorCap as))
            ;;48 is admissible, so the cap is exactly 49
            (expect "<<AQP-G35>> ...with 48 still admissible, so the cap is exactly 49"
                true
                (let ((ignore (update AQP-ANK.ANK|T|AssetAnchors as { "anchors-active" : 48 })))
                    (AQP-ANK.UEV_AssetAnchorCap as)))
        ]
    )
    (print "--- [AQP-G35 · 02 · FINDING: E-ANK is an object, not a label] ---")
    ;;FOUND while reading the failures above, pinned AS IT BEHAVES.
    ;;
    ;;Every one of these messages is built as `(format "{} BoostClass {} …" [E-ANK boost-class-id])`,
    ;;and `E-ANK` is NOT a label. 01_ANK.pact:292 defines it as the EMPTY-ANCHOR object:
    ;;    {"promile" : 0.0, "ouronet-account" : BAR, "anchor-id" : BAR}
    ;;so every message begins with that JSON. The caller reads:
    ;;    {"anchor-id": "|","ouronet-account": "|","promile": 0.0} BoostClass … must be active
    ;;
    ;;The intended shape is elsewhere in the codebase: DPOF defines `(defconst OF "Orto-Fungible")`
    ;;and its messages read "Orto-Fungible MOCKO-… Nonce 1 must be …". ANK has NO string label
    ;;constant, so whoever wrote these reached for the nearest `E-`-prefixed name and got the blank
    ;;row constructor instead. 7 uses of E-ANK in the module, all of them message prefixes.
    ;;
    ;;Fails safe -- the guard still blocks, and the informative half of the message is intact -- so
    ;;this is message quality, not behaviour. Same class as the missing `format` at 15_SWP.pact:466
    ;;(see SWP-G21), which was a one-token repair with no behavioural change. PROPOSED, not applied:
    ;;add a string label constant and use it in the 7 messages. Pinned here so the fix has a test
    ;;waiting: when the label becomes a string, this assertion fails and names itself.
    (map print
        [
            (expect "<<AQP-G35>> FINDING: E-ANK is the empty-anchor OBJECT, not a label string"
                {"promile" : 0.0, "ouronet-account" : (U|CT.CT_BAR), "anchor-id" : (U|CT.CT_BAR)}
                AQP-ANK.E-ANK)
            ;;...so the message a caller actually sees opens with that object's JSON
            (expect-failure "<<AQP-G35>> ...so every ANK rejection opens with an object dump"
                "{\"anchor-id\": \"|\",\"ouronet-account\": \"|\",\"promile\": 0.0} Asset"
                (let ((ignore (update AQP-ANK.ANK|T|AssetAnchors as { "anchors-active" : 49 })))
                    (AQP-ANK.UEV_AssetAnchorCap as)))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(rollback-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
