;;NOT PINNABLE ON THIS CHAIN, WITH THE REASON — AQP-SCORE's LP-stake context.
;;
;;`02_SCORE.pact:2708` "LP stake score context: pool-id, score-class, or LP pair vs lp-denominator
;;mismatch" (`UEV_LpStakeScoreContext`, unprotected and directly callable).
;;
;;ITS THREE CONJUNCTS ARE ALL SATISFIABLE-TO-FALSE HERE -- in particular `(= (UR_SCR|ScoreClass score-id)
;;0)` fails for EVERY score on this chain, because **none of the 37 scores is class 0** (measured). So the
;;argument side is free. What is missing is upstream of the conjuncts:
;;
;;    (native-lp:string (URC_StakeLpTokenToNativeLpDptf lp-id))
;;    (swpair:string    (ref-SWP::UR_GetLpSwpair native-lp))      <- hard read of SWP|LP
;;    (pool-tokens:[string] (ref-SWP::UR_PoolTokens swpair))
;;
;;This chain has NO SWP LP PAIRS: `UR_GetLpSwpair` on the suite's usual LP id answers
;;    No value found in table ouronet-ns.SWP_SWP|LP for key: S|DLK-…|OURO-…|DWK-…
;;so any lp-id argument dies in the `let` before a conjunct is evaluated. (Another instance of the shape
;;in 2026-09-12-eager-let-mute-guards.md, though here it is the FIXTURE that is missing rather than the
;;guard being at fault -- a real LP id would read fine.)
;;
;;WHAT IT WOULD TAKE: one chain carrying BOTH an SWP LP pair and an AQP score. No harness builds both
;;today -- `modules/SWP.repl` has the pools but not Stage-02, `modules/AQP.repl` has the scores but no
;;pools. Cheapest route is probably to add `[6.3]_SWP` (or the issuance-only variant) ahead of
;;`[6.2]_AQP` in a new loader, then point a class-0 score's lp-denominator at a token of that pair.
;;
;;Recorded rather than left as a bare worklist entry, because "needs a fixture" is not the useful part --
;;WHICH fixture, and why the obvious argument-only attempt fails, is.


