(begin-tx "AQP-G44 — the vacate class backstop, driven on a FORCED corrupt pool row")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [AQP-G44 · 01 · a pool row carrying an aqp-class outside 0-4] ---")
;;`06_VCT.pact:537` — `(enforce (contains (UR_AQP|PoolAqpClass pool-id) [0 1 2 3 4]) "VCT|C>VACATE:
;;unknown aqp-class")`. No client can produce the state it rejects: pool issuance validates the
;;class and no writer mutates it afterwards. So it is an INVARIANT BACKSTOP, and the rule for those
;;is to drive the invariant FALSE and execute the guard rather than annotate it as unreachable.
;;
;;WHY THIS BACKSTOP IS NOT DECORATIVE — the part actually worth recording. `URC_AqpOwnerKonto`, the
;;function the OWNER check on the line above runs, resolves the pool governor through an if-chain:
;;`0 → SWP LP, 1 → DPTF, 2 → DPOF, 3 → DPSF, else → DPNF`. That `else` carries no range check, so
;;class 9, class 400 and class -1 all resolve silently as DPNF. A corrupt row would therefore NOT be
;;stopped by the owner check — it would sail through it and be vacated AS THE WRONG CLASS, against
;;the wrong tracker tables. :537 is the only line standing in the way, and the assertions below show
;;precisely that: the owner check passes on the junk row, then the class enforce refuses it.
;;
;;THE ROW IS FORCED, NOT EARNED. `AQP-POOL.SECURE` is a trivially-true cap, so `WI_Pool` is reachable
;;with `test-capability` and no module-admin is needed. The asset is DHB, a REAL DPNF collection in
;;this suite — which is what makes the owner resolution meaningful rather than an abort on a missing
;;row, and it is why this transaction signs PK_Lumy: DHB's owner konto is Lumy's, not the patron's.
;;The whole block sits in a `rollback-tx`, so the junk pool never reaches a later assertion.
;;==== AQP-G44 — the vacate class backstop, driven on a FORCED corrupt pool row · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [AQP-G44 — the vacate class backstop, driven on a FORCED corrupt pool row · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] } { "key": "PK_Lumy", "caps": [] }])
;;==== AQP-G44 — the vacate class backstop, driven on a FORCED corrupt pool row · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [AQP-G44 — the vacate class backstop, driven on a FORCED corrupt pool row · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (ref-AQP:module{AcquisitionPoolsV1} AQP-POOL)
        (ref-DPDC:module{DpdcV2} DPDC)
        (ref-TS02-C3:module{TalosStageTwo_ClientThreeV1} TS02-C3)
        (junk:string "JunkClassPool-98c486052a51")
        (dhb:string "DHB-98c486052a51")
    )
    (test-capability (AQP-POOL.SECURE))
    (AQP-POOL.WI_Pool junk
        { "aqp-class"          : 9
        , "asset-id"           : dhb
        , "score-primary"      : "BAR"
        , "score-secondary"    : "BAR"
        , "score-tertiary"     : "BAR"
        , "score-quaternary"   : "BAR"
        , "score-quinary"      : "BAR"
        , "score-senary"       : "BAR"
        , "score-septenary"    : "BAR"
        , "stake-enabled"      : false
        , "vacate-in-progress" : false
        , "sweep-in-progress"  : false
        , "nns"                : 0
        , "aqp-id"             : junk
        }
    )
    (map print
        [
            (expect "<<AQP-G44>> the forced row really does carry a class outside 0-4"
                9 (ref-AQP::UR_AQP|PoolAqpClass junk))
            ;;THE POINT. The owner resolver does not reject class 9 — it falls out of the if-chain's
            ;;else branch and answers as though this were a class-4 DPNF pool, returning DHB's DPNF
            ;;owner konto verbatim. Asserted as an EQUALITY against the DPNF reader rather than
            ;;against a hardcoded principal, so it states the mechanism and not just a value.
            (expect "<<AQP-G44>> ...and the owner resolver silently answers it as a DPNF pool"
                (ref-DPDC::UR_OwnerKonto dhb false)
                (ref-AQP::URC_AqpOwnerKonto junk))
            (expect-failure "<<AQP-G44>> so the vacate is refused on the class alone, past the owner check"
                "VCT|C>VACATE: unknown aqp-class"
                (ref-TS02-C3::AQP-POOL|CC_FullVacate KST.ANHD junk))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
;;the forced row is discarded — no later assertion in this suite ever sees it.
(rollback-tx)

